    "summary": "I built a two-storey storage tower with two drawers, one on each storey. It's made of two north half hex bases stacked at (0,0) on levels 0 and 1. Each base has a drawer on its cut face. The top has a cover so you can set things on it. Open faces are closed with solid end caps, and lockJoints was run to bolt the joints. The full check passed with no rule errors, and the mesh-collision check came back clear. The build has 23 parts and needs about 1,229 g of filament and about 1,770 minutes to print. For display, I opened the upper drawer and put a bin of M3 screws in it, and set a roll of gaffer tape on the top cover. An electrical tape roll wouldn't fit in the drawer, so I left it out.",
    "outcome": "built"
